/*
  PDFRender - baseline TIFF decoding.

  Covers what a TIFF actually needs to be readable rather than the
  whole of TIFF 6, which is a family of formats rather than one: both
  byte orders, 1/2/4/8/16 bits per sample, greyscale either way round,
  RGB, palette, strips and tiles, the horizontal-differencing
  predictor, and the four compressions that matter - none, LZW,
  Deflate and PackBits.  Those three compressed forms are exactly the
  filters the PDF side already has, which is why TIFF costs so little
  here.

  Out: CCITT G3/G4 and JPEG-in-TIFF (which are whole codecs of their
  own), and floating-point or >16-bit samples.

